    <item>
      <title>GW1: The Point of No Return</title>
      <description>The final week has arrived, and we're podding IRL. Join us as we embark on the 2026/27 FPL season. Lots of angst and despair to still be had.

Kick off your 2026/27 FPL Season right with 25% off your first year when you pay annually for our Patreon! You get ad-free episodes / Discord access / prize league / more episodes / etc… https://www.patreon.com/1069944/join

And don’t forget to join the prize league / mug league!!! https://www.patreon.com/FMLFPL/posts/signup-for-prize-164652803

Chapters:


  00:00:00 Intro and Anus Slaps

  00:01:58 Do We Need to Revisit EDOT (Elliot Anderson) with Set Pieces and Recoveries?

  00:03:53 Szoboszlai: Avenues and Wisdom of the Crowd Situation

  00:10:25 Time to Talk About Isak, and Possibly No Haaland or Isak with Haaland

  00:17:54 Is Fading João Pedro Too Big a Bet, or Just the Right Amount of Bet, and a Little Morgan Rogers to Boot

  00:26:31 Welcome Calafiori to the Team, and Other Arsenal Picks — Also O'Reilly

  00:35:29 Is Brighton Still Good for Bench Boost GW1?

  00:40:44 Couple of Bench Boost Questions

  00:49:48 Coming Around on Thiago and Brentford

  00:56:48 Shaw vs. Maguire

  01:02:40 Ödegaard and Some Tzolis

  01:08:31 Jacquet: Huge Upside and a Risk

  01:10:15 Are We Still Out on Semenyo?

  01:13:25 Taking Some Questions from Discord: Exploitable Fixtures, Mbeumo vs. Wirtz vs. Semenyo, Finding DefCon Monsters, Hume and De Cuyper

  01:24:44 Back to Our GW1 Teams: What Decisions Do We Have Left?


FML FPL is supported by our Patrons at https://www.patreon.com/FMLFPL

Shoutout to Keivon and @kunning + @nycsaladlover on instagram for the studio, the camera, and for the computer

FML FPL is a Fantasy Premier League podcast hosted by Alon and Walsh, two veteran FPL managers riding the highs and lows of every Gameweek. Expect brutally honest reactions, fantasy football advice you probably shouldn’t follow, and full Gameweek therapy.

#FPL #FantasyPremierLeague #FPLPodcast #FantasyFootball
Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices</description>
