    <item>
      <title>Building Our FPL Teams From the Ground Up</title>
      <description>We're both fairly settled, which feels… odd. Maybe this weekend will change it all, but we have two versions of building very similar GW1 teams: one trying to stave off the early wildcard, and one embracing the early wildcard.

Kick off your 2026/27 FPL Season right with 25% off your first year when you pay annually for our Patreon! You get ad-free episodes / Discord access / prize league / more episodes / etc… https://www.patreon.com/1069944/join

And don’t forget to join the prize league / mug league!!! https://www.patreon.com/FMLFPL/posts/signup-for-prize-164652803

Chapters:


  00:00:00 Intro, Admin, Anus Slaps, App Review, and Census Talk

  00:04:25 Walsh's GW1 Team: Cheap at the Back

  00:06:59 A Little João Pedro Chat: Are Any FPL Forwards Worth It?

  00:10:14 Alon's GW1 Team: Forwards Are Out

  00:15:51 Thinking About Isak a Little Bit: £6.5 Million Cheaper Than Haaland

  00:19:09 The Midfield Guys Everyone Is Talking About: Szoboszlai and Morgan Gibbs-White, and Then Some Mbeumo and Wirtz

  00:31:54 Ndiaye vs. Le Fée vs. Kluivert and More: Set Pieces and Penalties Are Volume Games

  00:37:30 Back to Walsh's Cheap Defense: Setting Up for an Earlyish Wildcard

  00:45:32 Shaw and Maguire

  00:48:05 No Arsenal in Our Drafts Even Though They're the Best Team: Tsolis? Mosquera? Calafiori? Ben White?

  00:56:24 Back to Alon's Team: VVD, and Then Full Circle Back to Pascal Groß

  01:07:10 One Week Left: What Spots Are We Still Analyzing and Figuring Out


FML FPL is supported by our Patrons at https://www.patreon.com/FMLFPL

