    <item>
      <title>Midpriced FPL Picks (Part 2): Forwards and Defenders</title>
      <description>We ended up going team by team for defenders and then we threw in a couple of forwards at the end. We've now entered hyper speed mindfuck vortex for the 2026/27 FPL season. Let's go.

Kick off your 2026/27 FPL Season right with 25% off your first year when you pay annually for our Patreon! You get ad-free episodes / Discord access / prize league / more episodes / etc… https://www.patreon.com/1069944/join

Chapters:


  00:00:00 Intro and YouTube and People Watching Podcasts

  00:05:44 Defenders and Wrapping Our Heads Around What to Do with DefCons

  00:12:11 Starting the £5.0-5.5 Million Defender Train in Sunderland: Ballard, Alderete, and Mukiele

  00:14:47 Spurs: Porro, Van Hecke, VDV, Romero, and Danso

  00:23:06 Transposing Glasner's Palace Teams to His Current NFO Team: Milenkovic, Murillo, Neco Williams, Morato, and Possibly More

  00:31:04 Man United and Their Fixtures Are Irresistible: Maguire and Lisandro

  00:34:03 Manchester, But City: This Team Is a Whole Bunch of Dudes and We Don't Really Know Who's Gonna Start

  00:37:44 Liverpool Are Kind of a Mess but Also Have Some Very Attacking Fullbacks in Kerkez and Frimpong

  00:43:26 Leeds Next Up with Bijol and Our New Friend Tarik

  00:48:53 Everton with Branthwaite and Keane and O'Brien

  00:50:36 Palace Have Munoz and Richards and Canvot

  00:51:36 Heavy Palestra Interest for Alon: and a Million Other Chelsea Defenders

  00:55:15 Brighton and No Idea Who Is Gonna Play

  00:59:37 Finishing Up an Hour on £5.0-5.5 Defenders with the Reigning Champs of Arsenal: Calafiori, Hincapié, Ben White, and Mosquera

  01:05:52 Forwards List of £6.5-7.5 Million Is Just Not a Lot: Gyök &amp; Kai, João Pedro, Šeško, and Mateta

  01:16:14 And That Is a Pod: Plans for Budget Pod, Bunch of Fireside Chats Incoming, Here We Fucking Go


